Sval: remove Firefox's app menu button and the nav bar's post-tabs spacer

Sval's header draws neither. The menu bar holds the app menu's commands
and the notices button its update notices, and the header row is the
titlebar, so its empty stretches drag the window. PanelUI keeps running
for the panels it shows elsewhere, so its reads of the button tolerate
its absence, as do CustomizeMode's, and PanelUI.show, with no anchor to
open from, does nothing.
ConfirmationHint.show anchors a hint whose anchor is missing to the panel
toggle.

diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser.js b/browser/base/content/browser.js
index 79bfd49a06..04f0050157 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser.js
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser.js
@@ -4731,9 +4731,7 @@ var ConfirmationHint = {
   ) {
     // Sval: the header draws no app menu button, so its panel toggle takes
     // the hints Firefox anchors there.
-    if (anchor?.id == "PanelUI-menu-button") {
-      anchor = document.getElementById("sval-panel-button") ?? anchor;
-    }
+    anchor ??= document.getElementById("sval-panel-button");
 
     this._reset();
 
